    "heading": "Opportunity Attacks",
    "lineStart": 13412,
    "lineEnd": 13414
  },
  "section": "8.108",
  "rulesText": "You can make an Opportunity Attack when a creature that you can see leaves your reach using its action, its Bonus Action, its Reaction, or one of its speeds. To make the Opportunity Attack, take a Reaction to make one melee attack with a weapon or an Unarmed Strike against the provoking creature. The attack occurs right before the creature leaves your reach. See also “Playing the Game” (“Combat”)."
}
